name:In Processionibus extraordinariis: Et ne nos inducas; Ora pro nobis; Domine, non secundum (versus);
office-part:Versiculus;
mode:;
book:Processionarium O.P. (Cormier), 1913, p. 131 (text, each line ending with the flexa sign);
commentary:Versicle: Art. II § IV 3° (pp. 395-396: "Subscripto modo dicantur Versiculi ad Memorias et ante Laudes, et in Processionibus, et quotiescumque dicitur V. a Sacerdote"): tenor h, the syllables after the last accent of the versicle fall to f, as in the printed example Dignáre me laudáre te, Virgo sacráta. R. Da mihi virtútem contra hostes tuos (pp. 395-396). Proparoxytone endings: both syllables after the accent fall (geminatur nota re, p. 402). The fall is where pp. 131-134 print the flexa sign. F clef on the 3rd line as printed.;
transcriber:the tone printed in the Processionarium O.P. 1913 applied to this text for this site (the book prints this text without notes);
%%
(f3) <sp>V/</sp>. Et(h) ne(h) nos(h) in(h)dú(h)cas(h) in(h) ten(h)ta(h)ti(h)ó(h)nem.(f) (::) <sp>R/</sp>. Sed(h) lí(h)be(h)ra(h) nos(h) a(h) ma(h)lo.(f) (::) <sp>V/</sp>. O(h)ra(h) pro(h) no(h)bis,(h) san(h)cta(h) De(h)i(h) Gé(h)ni(f)trix.(f) (::) <sp>R/</sp>. Ut(h) di(h)gni(h) ef(h)fi(h)ci(h)á(h)mur(h) pro(h)mis(h)si(h)ó(h)ni(h)bus(h) Chri(h)sti.(f) (::) <sp>V/</sp>. Dó(h)mi(h)ne,(h) non(h) se(h)cún(h)dum(h) pec(h)cá(h)ta(h) nos(h)tra(h) fá(h)ci(h)as(h) no(h)bis.(f) (::) <sp>R/</sp>. Ne(h)que(h) se(h)cún(h)dum(h) i(h)ni(h)qui(h)tá(h)tes(h) nos(h)tras(h) re(h)trí(h)bu(h)as(h) no(h)bis.(f) (::)
